WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.080
- [Narrator] In this
video, we're gonna talk

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.820
about shapes and something called angles,

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.470
which you've might have
heard the word before.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:11.190
So the first question is what is an angle?

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.270
Well let me draw a shape
and that might help explain

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:15.550
what an angle is.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.380
So I'm gonna draw a triangle,

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.410
and you might already know that
a triangle has three sides.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.920
You can see one side,
two sides, three sides,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.470
but it also has three angles.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.700
Now, what are the angles?

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.400
Well for a shape like this, you can think

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.610
of an angle as where two
of the sides come together.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:38.190
So for example, this right
over here is an angle

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.410
because two of the sides
have come together there,

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.510
this side and this side
come together at that point.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.900
So that's an angle.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.640
This is another angle.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.180
And that's another angle.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.960
So not only does a
triangle have three sides,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.610
it also has three angles.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.040
Now let me ask you a question.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.810
If I had a rectangle like this,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:04.120
how many angles does it have?

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.920
Pause this video and think about it.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.770
Well, we can see the angles.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.780
We have one angle here,
another angle here,

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.410
so two, three and four.

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.650
So not only does a
rectangle have four sides,

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.010
it also has four angles.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.530
Now what if I were to give
you another four-sided figure

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.830
another quadrilateral,
quadrilateral's a very fancy word,

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.140
but it really just
means four-sided figure,

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.860
but one that's not a rectangle.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.810
What if I were to give
you something like this?

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.710
So this type of a quadrilateral,

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:40.000
it still has four sides,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.740
but you can see that it looks

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.300
a little bit different than a rectangle,

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.820
I can do it so it's pretty straight.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.500
It still has one, two, three, four sides.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.850
How many angles do we have?

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.920
And this figure is called a trapezoid.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.333
How many angles does a trapezoid have?

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.950
Well, let me count them again.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.690
So we have one angle right over here,

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:05.470
two, three, and four.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.700
So this quadrilateral, this trapezoid,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.700
like a rectangle, has both
four sides and four angles.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.735
Now, if I were to go the other way around,

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.740
if I were to ask you to draw a figure,

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.160
and if you have pencil and
paper I encourage you to do it,

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.300
try to draw a shape that has five angles

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.723
and see if you know the
name for that shape.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.010
All right, now let's
try to do this together

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.280
and let me do this in a fun color,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.010
watch I'll do it in purple.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:38.170
So that is one angle right over there,

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.060
then I have two angles,

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.150
then I have three angles,
and now I have four angles.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.010
And if I meet there, I get five angles.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.980
So we could see the angles here.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.980
I have one, two, three,
four, five angles here.

00:02:55.682 --> 00:03:00.560
You also might see that I have one, two,

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.190
three, four, five sides.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.430
And what do we call a five sided figure?

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:09.270
We call that a pentagon.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.410
This is a pentagon right over here.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:14.280
So five angles and we had five sides.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.430
And so you could imagine
if I had six angles,

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.130
what type of a figure would it be?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.400
Well, I might not even draw it,

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.880
you could draw it on paper if you like,

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.210
but if you had six angles,
you're going to have a hexagon,

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.493
which is a six sided figure.

